  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">HO-503001</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Escalation of violence in Gaza has left a significant number of civilians killed &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; wounded, with over 80% internally displaced. The violence has damaged shelters &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; infrastructure. The situation is becoming increasingly dire. Even before Oct-23, over 80% of Gazans needed humanitarian aid. Because of politically driven pressure, some donors have stopped/cut aid, creating severe service gaps. With the complete seize imposed, ppl. are struggling to secure cash to support their basic needs to buy food, water &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; medicine. Thousands have lost their homes and are now forced into temporary shelters, facing multiple protection risks. Shutdown of Gaza&apos;s power plant due to lack of fuel &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; hundreds of Israeli military airstrikes have destroyed essential WASH infrastructures &lt;(&gt;&amp;&lt;)&gt; public services.
Oxfam Novib launched a public appeal to support the affected people, and infrastructure and conduct advocacy efforts for longer-term and sustainable solutions to the crisis</narrative>
  </description>
  <participating-org ref="NL-KVK-27108436" role="4" type="21">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib was founded in 1956 as the Netherlands Organisation for International Assistance (Novib), and joined forces with Oxfam in 1994.  Oxfam Novib is member of the Oxfam International confederation. Working together in the confederation, the Oxfam affiliates can speak with one clear and compelling voice on issues of global concern: climate change, health and education for all, agriculture, trade, and conflicts and emergencies.  Oxfam Novib&apos;s main office is based in The Netherlands, it supports the work of a network of local offices, the implementation of global projects, fundraising, campaigning and advocacy.  Oxfam Novib&#x92;s the Hague office contributes towards this project&#x92;s implementation.</narrative>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Oxfam Novib</narrative>
  </participating-org>
